  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>Welcoming your dog</h2>
      <p>The hotel's official website, on its "Hotel" page, says: "Pets accepted and welcome". The Grimaud tourist office lists Le Verger Maelvi in its "Dog-friendly hotels" list, and the Visit Var page says "Pets accepted". The website publishes no surcharge, no limit on dog size or number, and no leash rule in the common areas.</p>

      <h2>The hotel</h2>
      <p>A Provençal residence at the foot of the medieval village of Grimaud, on the banks of the little river the Giscle and facing the Maures massif, the hotel has 4 stars. The rooms open onto flowery terraces and the landscaped garden, with a heated pool in the middle of the grounds. The website gives Grimaud beach at 7 km and Saint-Tropez at 10 km.</p>
      <p>On site: a free and secure car park 24 hours a day, with sheltered spaces to rent at €10 per day, a concierge open from 7am to midnight, light meals from 12pm to 4pm and room service from 8am to midnight. Breakfasts include a wide choice of organic products. The tourist office adds a tennis court, a gym and bike rental. The hotel is open from 1 April to 16 October 2026, every day, according to the tourist office.</p>

      <h2>Worth checking before you go</h2>
      <p>No surcharge or behaviour rule is published for dogs, and the number of rooms differs between sources (14 rooms and suites on the hotel website, 12 accommodations for the tourist office). Ask about the conditions by phone on 04 94 55 57 80 when booking. The 2027 opening dates are not yet published.</p>
